{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs | sed -n '300,510p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/mod.rs | head -260; grep -n 'fn\\\\|quorum' ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/util.rs | head -100; grep -n '\"'^#'\"\\\\|guide.md\\\\|behavior-facts' ../audit-method.md\"","aggregated_output":"   300\t\n   301\t    pub(crate) fn handle_promise_accept(&mut self, prom: Promise<T>, from: NodeId) {\n   302\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   303\t        {\n   304\t            let (r, p) = &self.state;\n   305\t            debug!(\n   306\t                self.logger,\n   307\t                \"Self role {:?}, phase {:?}. Incoming message Promise Accept from {}\", r, p, from\n   308\t            );\n   309\t        }\n   310\t        if prom.n == self.leader_state.n_leader {\n   311\t            self.leader_state.set_promise(prom, from, false);\n   312\t            self.send_accsync(from);\n   313\t        }\n   314\t    }\n   315\t\n   316\t    pub(crate) fn handle_accepted(&mut self, accepted: Accepted, from: NodeId) {\n   317\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   318\t        trace!(\n   319\t            self.logger,\n   320\t            \"Got Accepted from {}, idx: {}, chosen_idx: {}, accepted: {:?}\",\n   321\t            from,\n   322\t            accepted.accepted_idx,\n   323\t            self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx(),\n   324\t            self.leader_state.accepted_indexes\n   325\t        );\n   326\t        if accepted.n == self.leader_state.n_leader && self.state == (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) {\n   327\t            self.leader_state\n   328\t                .set_accepted_idx(from, accepted.accepted_idx);\n   329\t            if accepted.accepted_idx > self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx()\n   330\t                && self.leader_state.is_chosen(accepted.accepted_idx)\n   331\t            {\n   332\t                let decided_idx = accepted.accepted_idx;\n   333\t                self.internal_storage\n   334\t                    .set_decided_idx(decided_idx)\n   335\t                    .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n   336\t                for pid in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n   337\t                    let latest_accdec = self.get_latest_accdec_message(pid);\n   338\t                    match latest_accdec {\n   339\t                        Some(accdec) => accdec.decided_idx = decided_idx,\n   340\t                        None => self.send_decide(pid, decided_idx, false),\n   341\t                    }\n   342\t                }\n   343\t            }\n   344\t        }\n   345\t    }\n   346\t\n   347\t    fn get_latest_accdec_message(&mut self, to: NodeId) -> Option<&mut AcceptDecide<T>> {\n   348\t        if let Some((bal, outgoing_idx)) = self.leader_state.get_latest_accept_meta(to) {\n   349\t            if bal == self.leader_state.n_leader {\n   350\t                if let Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n   351\t                    msg: PaxosMsg::AcceptDecide(accdec),\n   352\t                    ..\n   353\t                }) = self.outgoing.get_mut(outgoing_idx).unwrap()\n   354\t                {\n   355\t                    return Some(accdec);\n   356\t                } else {\n   357\t                    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   358\t                    debug!(self.logger, \"Cached idx is not an AcceptedDecide!\");\n   359\t                }\n   360\t            }\n   361\t        }\n   362\t        None\n   363\t    }\n   364\t\n   365\t    pub(crate) fn handle_notaccepted(&mut self, not_acc: NotAccepted, from: NodeId) {\n   366\t        if self.state.0 == Role::Leader && self.leader_state.n_leader < not_acc.n {\n   367\t            self.leader_state.lost_promise(from);\n   368\t        }\n   369\t    }\n   370\t\n   371\t    pub(crate) fn resend_messages_leader(&mut self) {\n   372\t        match self.state.1 {\n   373\t            Phase::Prepare => {\n   374\t                // Resend Prepare\n   375\t                let preparable_peers = self.leader_state.get_preparable_peers(&self.peers);\n   376\t                for peer in preparable_peers {\n   377\t                    self.send_prepare(peer);\n   378\t                }\n   379\t            }\n   380\t            Phase::Accept => {\n   381\t                // Resend AcceptStopSign or StopSign's decide\n   382\t                if let Some(ss) = self.internal_storage.get_stopsign() {\n   383\t                    let decided_idx = self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx();\n   384\t                    for follower in self.leader_state.get_promised_followers() {\n   385\t                        if self.internal_storage.stopsign_is_decided() {\n   386\t                            self.send_decide(follower, decided_idx, true);\n   387\t                        } else if self.leader_state.get_accepted_idx(follower)\n   388\t                            != self.internal_storage.get_accepted_idx()\n   389\t                        {\n   390\t                            self.send_accept_stopsign(follower, ss.clone(), true);\n   391\t                        }\n   392\t                    }\n   393\t                }\n   394\t                // Resend Prepare\n   395\t                let preparable_peers = self.leader_state.get_preparable_peers(&self.peers);\n   396\t                for peer in preparable_peers {\n   397\t                    self.send_prepare(peer);\n   398\t                }\n   399\t            }\n   400\t            Phase::Recover => (),\n   401\t            Phase::None => (),\n   402\t        }\n   403\t    }\n   404\t\n   405\t    pub(crate) fn flush_batch_leader(&mut self) {\n   406\t        let accepted_metadata = self\n   407\t            .internal_storage\n   408\t            .flush_batch_and_get_entries()\n   409\t            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n   410\t        if let Some(metadata) = accepted_metadata {\n   411\t            self.leader_state\n   412\t                .set_accepted_idx(self.pid, metadata.accepted_idx);\n   413\t            self.send_acceptdecide(metadata);\n   414\t        }\n   415\t    }\n   416\t}\n     1\tuse super::{ballot_leader_election::Ballot, messages::sequence_paxos::*, util::LeaderState};\n     2\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n     3\tuse crate::utils::logger::create_logger;\n     4\tuse crate::{\n     5\t    messages::Message,\n     6\t    storage::{\n     7\t        internal_storage::{InternalStorage, InternalStorageConfig},\n     8\t        Entry, Snapshot, StopSign, Storage,\n     9\t    },\n    10\t    util::{\n    11\t        FlexibleQuorum, LogSync, NodeId, Quorum, SequenceNumber, READ_ERROR_MSG, WRITE_ERROR_MSG,\n    12\t    },\n    13\t    ClusterConfig, CompactionErr, OmniPaxosConfig, ProposeErr,\n    14\t};\n    15\t#[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    16\tuse slog::{debug, info, trace, warn, Logger};\n    17\tuse std::{fmt::Debug, vec};\n    18\t\n    19\tpub mod follower;\n    20\tpub mod leader;\n    21\t\n    22\t/// a Sequence Paxos replica. Maintains local state of the replicated log, handles incoming messages and produces outgoing messages that the user has to fetch periodically and send using a network implementation.\n    23\t/// User also has to periodically fetch the decided entries that are guaranteed to be strongly consistent and linearizable, and therefore also safe to be used in the higher level application.\n    24\t/// If snapshots are not desired to be used, use `()` for the type parameter `S`.\n    25\tpub(crate) struct SequencePaxos<T, B>\n    26\twhere\n    27\t    T: Entry,\n    28\t    B: Storage<T>,\n    29\t{\n    30\t    pub(crate) internal_storage: InternalStorage<B, T>,\n    31\t    pid: NodeId,\n    32\t    peers: Vec<NodeId>, // excluding self pid\n    33\t    state: (Role, Phase),\n    34\t    buffered_proposals: Vec<T>,\n    35\t    buffered_stopsign: Option<StopSign>,\n    36\t    outgoing: Vec<Message<T>>,\n    37\t    leader_state: LeaderState<T>,\n    38\t    latest_accepted_meta: Option<(Ballot, usize)>,\n    39\t    // Keeps track of sequence of accepts from leader where AcceptSync = 1\n    40\t    current_seq_num: SequenceNumber,\n    41\t    cached_promise_message: Option<Promise<T>>,\n    42\t    #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n    43\t    logger: Logger,\n    44\t}\n    45\t\n    46\timpl<T, B> SequencePaxos<T, B>\n    47\twhere\n    48\t    T: Entry,\n    49\t    B: Storage<T>,\n    50\t{\n    51\t    /*** User functions ***/\n    52\t    /// Creates a Sequence Paxos replica.\n    53\t    pub(crate) fn with(config: SequencePaxosConfig, storage: B) -> Self {\n    54\t        let pid = config.pid;\n    55\t        let peers = config.peers;\n    56\t        let num_nodes = &peers.len() + 1;\n    57\t        let quorum = Quorum::with(config.flexible_quorum, num_nodes);\n    58\t        let max_peer_pid = peers.iter().max().unwrap();\n    59\t        let max_pid = *std::cmp::max(max_peer_pid, &pid) as usize;\n    60\t        let mut outgoing = Vec::with_capacity(config.buffer_size);\n    61\t        let (state, leader) = match storage\n    62\t            .get_promise()\n    63\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read promise\")\n    64\t        {\n    65\t            // if we recover a promise from storage then we must do failure recovery\n    66\t            Some(b) => {\n    67\t                let state = (Role::Follower, Phase::Recover);\n    68\t                for peer_pid in &peers {\n    69\t                    let prepreq = PrepareReq { n: b };\n    70\t                    outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n    71\t                        from: pid,\n    72\t                        to: *peer_pid,\n    73\t                        msg: PaxosMsg::PrepareReq(prepreq),\n    74\t                    }));\n    75\t                }\n    76\t                (state, b)\n    77\t            }\n    78\t            None => ((Role::Follower, Phase::None), Ballot::default()),\n    79\t        };\n    80\t        let internal_storage_config = InternalStorageConfig {\n    81\t            batch_size: config.batch_size,\n    82\t        };\n    83\t        let mut paxos = SequencePaxos {\n    84\t            internal_storage: InternalStorage::with(\n    85\t                storage,\n    86\t                internal_storage_config,\n    87\t                #[cfg(feature = \"unicache\")]\n    88\t                pid,\n    89\t            ),\n    90\t            pid,\n    91\t            peers,\n    92\t            state,\n    93\t            buffered_proposals: vec![],\n    94\t            buffered_stopsign: None,\n    95\t            outgoing,\n    96\t            leader_state: LeaderState::<T>::with(leader, max_pid, quorum),\n    97\t            latest_accepted_meta: None,\n    98\t            current_seq_num: SequenceNumber::default(),\n    99\t            cached_promise_message: None,\n   100\t            #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   101\t            logger: {\n   102\t                if let Some(logger) = config.custom_logger {\n   103\t                    logger\n   104\t                } else {\n   105\t                    let s = config\n   106\t                        .logger_file_path\n   107\t                        .unwrap_or_else(|| format!(\"logs/paxos_{}.log\", pid));\n   108\t                    create_logger(s.as_str())\n   109\t                }\n   110\t            },\n   111\t        };\n   112\t        paxos\n   113\t            .internal_storage\n   114\t            .set_promise(leader)\n   115\t            .expect(WRITE_ERROR_MSG);\n   116\t        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   117\t        {\n   118\t            info!(paxos.logger, \"Paxos component pid: {} created!\", pid);\n   119\t            if let Quorum::Flexible(flex_quorum) = quorum {\n   120\t                if flex_quorum.read_quorum_size > num_nodes - flex_quorum.write_quorum_size + 1 {\n   121\t                    warn!(\n   122\t                        paxos.logger,\n   123\t                        \"Unnecessary overlaps in read and write quorums. Read and Write quorums only need to be overlapping by one node i.e., read_quorum_size + write_quorum_size = num_nodes + 1\");\n   124\t                }\n   125\t            }\n   126\t        }\n   127\t        paxos\n   128\t    }\n   129\t\n   130\t    pub(crate) fn get_state(&self) -> &(Role, Phase) {\n   131\t        &self.state\n   132\t    }\n   133\t\n   134\t    pub(crate) fn get_promise(&self) -> Ballot {\n   135\t        self.internal_storage.get_promise()\n   136\t    }\n   137\t\n   138\t    /// Initiates the trim process.\n   139\t    /// # Arguments\n   140\t    /// * `trim_idx` - Deletes all entries up to [`trim_idx`], if the [`trim_idx`] is `None` then the minimum index accepted by **ALL** servers will be used as the [`trim_idx`].\n   141\t    pub(crate) fn trim(&mut self, trim_idx: Option<usize>) -> Result<(), CompactionErr> {\n   142\t        match self.state {\n   143\t            (Role::Leader, _) => {\n   144\t                let min_all_accepted_idx = self.leader_state.get_min_all_accepted_idx();\n   145\t                let trimmed_idx = match trim_idx {\n   146\t                    Some(idx) if idx <= *min_all_accepted_idx => idx,\n   147\t                    None => {\n   148\t                        #[cfg(feature = \"logging\")]\n   149\t                        trace!(\n   150\t                            self.logger,\n   151\t                            \"No trim index provided, using min_las_idx: {:?}\",\n   152\t                            min_all_accepted_idx\n   153\t                        );\n   154\t                        *min_all_accepted_idx\n   155\t                    }\n   156\t                    _ => {\n   157\t                        return Err(CompactionErr::NotAllDecided(*min_all_accepted_idx));\n   158\t                    }\n   159\t                };\n   160\t                let result = self.internal_storage.try_trim(trimmed_idx);\n   161\t                if result.is_ok() {\n   162\t                    for pid in &self.peers {\n   163\t                        let msg = PaxosMsg::Compaction(Compaction::Trim(trimmed_idx));\n   164\t                        self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n   165\t                            from: self.pid,\n   166\t                            to: *pid,\n   167\t                            msg,\n   168\t                        }));\n   169\t                    }\n   170\t                }\n   171\t                result.map_err(|e| {\n   172\t                    *e.downcast()\n   173\t                        .expect(\"storage error while trying to trim log\")\n   174\t                })\n   175\t            }\n   176\t            _ => Err(CompactionErr::NotCurrentLeader(self.get_current_leader())),\n   177\t        }\n   178\t    }\n   179\t\n   180\t    /// Trim the log and create a snapshot. ** Note: only up to the `decided_idx` can be snapshotted **\n   181\t    /// # Arguments\n   182\t    /// `idx` - Snapshots all entries with index < [`idx`], if the [`idx`] is None then the decided index will be used.\n   183\t    /// `local_only` - If `true`, only this server snapshots the log. If `false` all servers performs the snapshot.\n   184\t    pub(crate) fn snapshot(\n   185\t        &mut self,\n   186\t        idx: Option<usize>,\n   187\t        local_only: bool,\n   188\t    ) -> Result<(), CompactionErr> {\n   189\t        let result = self.internal_storage.try_snapshot(idx);\n   190\t        if !local_only && result.is_ok() {\n   191\t            // since it is decided, it is ok even for a follower to send this\n   192\t            for pid in &self.peers {\n   193\t                let msg = PaxosMsg::Compaction(Compaction::Snapshot(idx));\n   194\t                self.outgoing.push(Message::SequencePaxos(PaxosMessage {\n   195\t                    from: self.pid,\n   196\t                    to: *pid,\n   197\t                    msg,\n   198\t                }));\n   199\t            }\n   200\t        }\n   201\t        result.map_err(|e| {\n   202\t            *e.downcast()\n   203\t                .expect(\"storage error while trying to snapshot log\")\n   204\t        })\n   205\t    }\n   206\t\n   207\t    /// Return the decided index.\n   208\t    pub(crate) fn get_decided_idx(&self) -> usize {\n   209\t        self.internal_storage.get_decided_idx()\n   210\t    }\n   211\t\n   212\t    /// Return trim index from storage.\n   213\t    pub(crate) fn get_compacted_idx(&self) -> usize {\n   214\t        self.internal_storage.get_compacted_idx()\n   215\t    }\n   216\t\n   217\t    fn handle_compaction(&mut self, c: Compaction) {\n   218\t        // try trimming and snapshotting forwarded compaction. Errors are ignored as that the data will still be kept.\n   219\t        match c {\n   220\t            Compaction::Trim(idx) => {\n   221\t                let _ = self.internal_storage.try_trim(idx);\n   222\t            }\n   223\t            Compaction::Snapshot(idx) => {\n   224\t                let _ = self.snapshot(idx, true);\n   225\t            }\n   226\t        }\n   227\t    }\n   228\t\n   229\t    /// Detects if a Prepare, Promise, AcceptStopSign, Decide of a Stopsign, or PrepareReq message\n   230\t    /// has been sent but not been received. If so resends them. Note: We can't detect if a\n   231\t    /// StopSign's Decide message has been received so we always resend to be safe.\n   232\t    pub(crate) fn resend_message_timeout(&mut self) {\n   233\t        match self.state.0 {\n   234\t            Role::Leader => self.resend_messages_leader(),\n   235\t            Role::Follower => self.resend_messages_follower(),\n   236\t        }\n   237\t    }\n   238\t\n   239\t    /// Flushes any batched log entries and sends their corresponding Accept or Accepted messages.\n   240\t    pub(crate) fn flush_batch_timeout(&mut self) {\n   241\t        match self.state {\n   242\t            (Role::Leader, Phase::Accept) => self.flush_batch_leader(),\n   243\t            (Role::Follower, Phase::Accept) => self.flush_batch_follower(),\n   244\t            _ => (),\n   245\t        }\n   246\t    }\n   247\t\n   248\t    /// Moves the outgoing messages from this replica into the buffer. The messages should then be sent via the network implementation.\n   249\t    /// If `buffer` is empty, it gets swapped with the internal message buffer. Otherwise, messages are appended to the buffer. This prevents messages from getting discarded.\n   250\t    /// the buffer.\n   251\t    pub(crate) fn take_outgoing_msgs(&mut self, buffer: &mut Vec<Message<T>>) {\n   252\t        if buffer.is_empty() {\n   253\t            std::mem::swap(buffer, &mut self.outgoing);\n   254\t        } else {\n   255\t            // User has unsent messages in their buffer, must extend their buffer.\n   256\t            buffer.append(&mut self.outgoing);\n   257\t        }\n   258\t        self.leader_state.reset_latest_accept_meta();\n   259\t        self.latest_accepted_meta = None;\n   260\t    }\n37:    fn partial_cmp(&self, other: &Self) -> Option<Ordering> {\n55:    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n89:    pub quorum: Quorum,\n96:    pub fn with(n_leader: Ballot, max_pid: usize, quorum: Quorum) -> Self {\n106:            quorum,\n110:    fn pid_to_idx(pid: NodeId) -> usize {\n115:    pub fn increment_seq_num_session(&mut self, pid: NodeId) {\n121:    pub fn next_seq_num(&mut self, pid: NodeId) -> SequenceNumber {\n127:    pub fn get_seq_num(&mut self, pid: NodeId) -> SequenceNumber {\n131:    pub fn set_promise(&mut self, prom: Promise<T>, from: NodeId, check_max_prom: bool) -> bool {\n148:        self.quorum.is_prepare_quorum(num_promised)\n151:    pub fn reset_promise(&mut self, pid: NodeId) {\n156:    pub fn lost_promise(&mut self, pid: NodeId) {\n160:    pub fn take_max_promise_sync(&mut self) -> Option<LogSync<T>> {\n164:    pub fn get_max_promise_meta(&self) -> &PromiseMetaData {\n168:    pub fn get_max_decided_idx(&self) -> usize {\n179:    pub fn get_promise_meta(&self, pid: NodeId) -> &PromiseMetaData {\n186:    pub fn get_min_all_accepted_idx(&self) -> &usize {\n193:    pub fn reset_latest_accept_meta(&mut self) {\n197:    pub fn get_promised_followers(&self) -> Vec<NodeId> {\n211:    pub(crate) fn get_preparable_peers(&self, peers: &[NodeId]) -> Vec<NodeId> {\n224:    pub fn set_latest_accept_meta(&mut self, pid: NodeId, idx: Option<usize>) {\n229:    pub fn set_accepted_idx(&mut self, pid: NodeId, idx: usize) {\n233:    pub fn get_latest_accept_meta(&self, pid: NodeId) -> Option<(Ballot, usize)> {\n241:    pub fn get_decided_idx(&self, pid: NodeId) -> Option<usize> {\n248:    pub fn get_accepted_idx(&self, pid: NodeId) -> usize {\n252:    pub fn is_chosen(&self, idx: usize) -> bool {\n258:        self.quorum.is_accept_quorum(num_accepted)\n285:    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n320:    pub(crate) fn with(trimmed_idx: usize, snapshot: T::Snapshot) -> Self {\n333:    fn eq(&self, other: &Self) -> bool {\n382:    pub(crate) fn check_msg_status(&self, msg_seq_num: SequenceNumber) -> MessageStatus {\n399:    pub fn with(timeout: u64) -> Self {\n403:    pub fn tick_and_check_timeout(&mut self) -> bool {\n414:/// Flexible quorums can be used to increase/decrease the read and write quorum sizes,\n421:    pub read_quorum_size: usize,\n423:    pub write_quorum_size: usize,\n426:/// The type of quorum used by the OmniPaxos cluster.\n429:    /// Both the read quorum and the write quorums are a majority of nodes\n431:    /// The read and write quorum sizes are defined by a `FlexibleQuorum`\n436:    pub(crate) fn with(flexible_quorum_config: Option<FlexibleQuorum>, num_nodes: usize) -> Self {\n437:        match flexible_quorum_config {\n439:                read_quorum_size,\n440:                write_quorum_size,\n442:                read_quorum_size,\n443:                write_quorum_size,\n449:    pub(crate) fn is_prepare_quorum(&self, num_nodes: usize) -> bool {\n452:            Quorum::Flexible(flex_quorum) => num_nodes >= flex_quorum.read_quorum_size,\n456:    pub(crate) fn is_accept_quorum(&self, num_nodes: usize) -> bool {\n459:            Quorum::Flexible(flex_quorum) => num_nodes >= flex_quorum.write_quorum_size,\n479:    fn preparable_peers_test() {\n487:        let quorum = Quorum::Majority(2);\n490:            LeaderState::<Value>::with(Ballot::with(1, 1, 1, max_pid), max_pid as usize, quorum);\n495:        let quorum = Quorum::Majority(3);\n498:            LeaderState::<Value>::with(Ballot::with(1, 1, 1, max_pid), max_pid as usize, quorum);\n13:Follow guide.md using the controller's activity_roles. No preset protocol API or historical bug is required. Behavior/fact analysis and tool choice serve the selected discriminator.\n15:# Investigation and selection\n23:Use behavior-facts.md for implementation meaning. Select a principal Fact lifecycle with a sourced A1/A2 connection; a question need not span both. Direct behavior_ids establish, consume, invalidate or reinterpret it; supporting_behavior_ids explain separate history/context/consequence support. Cross-activity effects establish actual relationships without relabeling support Activities. Names and protocol labels establish neither relevance nor responsibility.\n33:At natural handoffs retain the answered proposition and remaining discriminator in feedback using tasks/audit.md references. In the next already-needed related map submission, replace the answered original unknown with its sourced conditional relationship and remove obsolete progress reminders. Correct materially misleading higher-level summaries in that same product before reuse; harmless wording differences need no cleanup turn or whole-map sweep. Preserve independent unknowns and historical inputs. Consult the actual answer and assessment, not an understanding label or reference alone. Use behavior-facts.md for primary ownership instead of copying one answer across layers. Source work and exploration may continue from feedback; near expiry save minimal complete learning.\n37:# Activity roles\n45:# Conditions, effects and semantic facts\n64:# evidence-review\n66:Use [guide.md](guide.md). Only controller-loaded references are available; links do not grant file access. Use Codex tools for missing authorized source; submit a typed research product only when ready for validation.\n87:# File products for one audit investigation\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"The handlers tie decision formation to ballot authority: the leader collects promises, synchronizes the selected log, then counts acknowledgments for its ballot. Followers reject stale ballots and use sequence numbers to detect gaps. I’ll trace quorum accounting, recovery, and caller duties before treating any local discrepancy as a defect.\n"}}
