{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs | sed -n '315,430p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs | sed -n '300,395p'; nl -ba ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md | head -100; nl -ba ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/storage.md | head -80; nl -ba ../agent-source/docs/omnipaxos/log.md | head -90\"","aggregated_output":"   315\t    pub fn take_outgoing_messages(&mut self, buffer: &mut Vec<Message<T>>) {\n   316\t        self.seq_paxos.take_outgoing_msgs(buffer);\n   317\t        buffer.extend(self.ble.outgoing_mut().drain(..).map(|b| Message::BLE(b)));\n   318\t    }\n   319\t\n   320\t    /// Read entry at index `idx` in the log. Returns `None` if `idx` is out of bounds.\n   321\t    pub fn read(&self, idx: usize) -> Option<LogEntry<T>> {\n   322\t        match self\n   323\t            .seq_paxos\n   324\t            .internal_storage\n   325\t            .read(idx..idx + 1)\n   326\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read log entries\")\n   327\t        {\n   328\t            Some(mut v) => v.pop(),\n   329\t            None => None,\n   330\t        }\n   331\t    }\n   332\t\n   333\t    /// Read entries in the range `r` in the log. Returns `None` if `r` is out of bounds.\n   334\t    pub fn read_entries<R>(&self, r: R) -> Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>>\n   335\t    where\n   336\t        R: RangeBounds<usize>,\n   337\t    {\n   338\t        self.seq_paxos\n   339\t            .internal_storage\n   340\t            .read(r)\n   341\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read log entries\")\n   342\t    }\n   343\t\n   344\t    /// Read all decided entries starting at `from_idx` (inclusive) in the log. Returns `None` if `from_idx` is out of bounds.\n   345\t    pub fn read_decided_suffix(&self, from_idx: usize) -> Option<Vec<LogEntry<T>>> {\n   346\t        self.seq_paxos\n   347\t            .internal_storage\n   348\t            .read_decided_suffix(from_idx)\n   349\t            .expect(\"storage error while trying to read decided log suffix\")\n   350\t    }\n   351\t\n   352\t    /// Handle an incoming message\n   353\t    pub fn handle_incoming(&mut self, m: Message<T>) {\n   354\t        match m {\n   355\t            Message::SequencePaxos(p) => self.seq_paxos.handle(p),\n   356\t            Message::BLE(b) => self.ble.handle(b),\n   357\t            #[cfg(feature = \"async_runtime\")]\n   358\t            Message::AsyncRuntime(_) => {\n   359\t                // Runtime-layer messages are consumed by the actor before reaching here.\n   360\t                // If one leaks through (e.g. user hand-delivered), silently ignore.\n   361\t            }\n   362\t        }\n   363\t    }\n   364\t\n   365\t    /// Returns whether this Sequence Paxos has been reconfigured\n   366\t    pub fn is_reconfigured(&self) -> Option<StopSign> {\n   367\t        self.seq_paxos.is_reconfigured()\n   368\t    }\n   369\t\n   370\t    /// Append an entry to the replicated log.\n   371\t    pub fn append(&mut self, entry: T) -> Result<(), ProposeErr<T>> {\n   372\t        self.seq_paxos.append(entry)\n   373\t    }\n   374\t\n   375\t    /// Propose a cluster reconfiguration. Returns an error if the current configuration has already been stopped\n   376\t    /// by a previous reconfiguration request or if the `new_configuration` is invalid.\n   377\t    /// `new_configuration` defines the cluster-wide configuration settings for the **next** cluster.\n   378\t    /// `metadata` is optional data to commit alongside the reconfiguration.\n   379\t    pub fn reconfigure(\n   380\t        &mut self,\n   381\t        new_configuration: ClusterConfig,\n   382\t        metadata: Option<Vec<u8>>,\n   383\t    ) -> Result<(), ProposeErr<T>> {\n   384\t        if let Err(config_error) = new_configuration.validate() {\n   385\t            return Err(ProposeErr::ConfigError(\n   386\t                config_error,\n   387\t                new_configuration,\n   388\t                metadata,\n   389\t            ));\n   390\t        }\n   391\t        self.seq_paxos.reconfigure(new_configuration, metadata)\n   392\t    }\n   393\t\n   394\t    /// Handles re-establishing a connection to a previously disconnected peer.\n   395\t    /// This should only be called if the underlying network implementation indicates that a connection has been re-established.\n   396\t    pub fn reconnected(&mut self, pid: NodeId) {\n   397\t        self.seq_paxos.reconnected(pid)\n   398\t    }\n   399\t\n   400\t    /// Increments the internal logical clock. This drives the processes for leader changes, resending dropped messages, and flushing batched log entries.\n   401\t    /// Each of these is triggered every `election_tick_timeout`, `resend_message_tick_timeout`, and `flush_batch_tick_timeout` number of calls to this function\n   402\t    /// (See how to configure these timeouts in `ServerConfig`).\n   403\t    pub fn tick(&mut self) {\n   404\t        if self.election_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   405\t            self.election_timeout();\n   406\t        }\n   407\t        if self.resend_message_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   408\t            self.seq_paxos.resend_message_timeout();\n   409\t        }\n   410\t        if self.flush_batch_clock.tick_and_check_timeout() {\n   411\t            self.seq_paxos.flush_batch_timeout();\n   412\t        }\n   413\t    }\n   414\t\n   415\t    /// Manually attempt to become the leader by incrementing this instance's Ballot. Calling this\n   416\t    /// function may not result in gainig leadership if other instances are competing for\n   417\t    /// leadership with higher Ballots.\n   418\t    pub fn try_become_leader(&mut self) {\n   419\t        let mut my_ballot = self.ble.get_current_ballot();\n   420\t        let promise = self.seq_paxos.get_promise();\n   421\t        my_ballot.n = promise.n + 1;\n   422\t        self.seq_paxos.handle_leader(my_ballot);\n   423\t    }\n   424\t\n   425\t    /*** BLE calls ***/\n   426\t    /// Update the custom priority used in the Ballot for this server. Note that changing the\n   427\t    /// priority triggers a leader re-election.\n   428\t    pub fn set_priority(&mut self, p: u32) {\n   429\t        self.ble.set_priority(p)\n   430\t    }\n   300\t    }\n   301\t\n   302\t    // Append entries without batching, return the accepted index\n   303\t    pub(crate) fn append_entries_without_batching(\n   304\t        &mut self,\n   305\t        entries: Vec<T>,\n   306\t    ) -> StorageResult<usize> {\n   307\t        let num_new_entries = entries.len();\n   308\t        self.storage.append_entries(entries)?;\n   309\t        self.state_cache.accepted_idx += num_new_entries;\n   310\t        Ok(self.state_cache.accepted_idx)\n   311\t    }\n   312\t\n   313\t    pub(crate) fn sync_log(\n   314\t        &mut self,\n   315\t        accepted_round: Ballot,\n   316\t        decided_idx: usize,\n   317\t        log_sync: Option<LogSync<T>>,\n   318\t    ) -> StorageResult<usize> {\n   319\t        self.state_cache.accepted_round = accepted_round;\n   320\t        self.state_cache.decided_idx = decided_idx;\n   321\t        let mut sync_txn: Vec<StorageOp<T>> = vec![\n   322\t            StorageOp::SetAcceptedRound(accepted_round),\n   323\t            StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(decided_idx),\n   324\t        ];\n   325\t        if let Some(sync) = log_sync {\n   326\t            match sync.decided_snapshot {\n   327\t                Some(SnapshotType::Complete(c)) => {\n   328\t                    self.state_cache.compacted_idx = sync.sync_idx;\n   329\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::Trim(sync.sync_idx));\n   330\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetCompactedIdx(sync.sync_idx));\n   331\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetSnapshot(Some(c)));\n   332\t                }\n   333\t                Some(SnapshotType::Delta(d)) => {\n   334\t                    let mut snapshot = self.create_decided_snapshot()?;\n   335\t                    snapshot.merge(d);\n   336\t                    self.state_cache.compacted_idx = sync.sync_idx;\n   337\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::Trim(sync.sync_idx));\n   338\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetCompactedIdx(sync.sync_idx));\n   339\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetSnapshot(Some(snapshot)));\n   340\t                }\n   341\t                None => (),\n   342\t            }\n   343\t            self.state_cache.accepted_idx = sync.sync_idx + sync.suffix.len();\n   344\t            sync_txn.push(StorageOp::AppendOnPrefix(sync.sync_idx, sync.suffix));\n   345\t            match sync.stopsign {\n   346\t                Some(ss) => {\n   347\t                    self.state_cache.stopsign = Some(ss.clone());\n   348\t                    self.state_cache.accepted_idx += 1;\n   349\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetStopsign(Some(ss)));\n   350\t                }\n   351\t                None if self.state_cache.stopsign.is_some() => {\n   352\t                    self.state_cache.stopsign = None;\n   353\t                    sync_txn.push(StorageOp::SetStopsign(None));\n   354\t                }\n   355\t                None => (),\n   356\t            }\n   357\t        }\n   358\t        self.storage.write_atomically(sync_txn)?;\n   359\t        Ok(self.state_cache.accepted_idx)\n   360\t    }\n   361\t\n   362\t    fn create_decided_snapshot(&mut self) -> StorageResult<T::Snapshot> {\n   363\t        let log_decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx_without_stopsign();\n   364\t        self.create_snapshot(log_decided_idx)\n   365\t    }\n   366\t\n   367\t    pub(crate) fn create_snapshot(&self, compact_idx: usize) -> StorageResult<T::Snapshot> {\n   368\t        let current_compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n   369\t        if compact_idx < current_compacted_idx {\n   370\t            Err(CompactionErr::TrimmedIndex(current_compacted_idx))?\n   371\t        }\n   372\t        let entries = self\n   373\t            .storage\n   374\t            .get_entries(current_compacted_idx, compact_idx)?;\n   375\t        let delta = T::Snapshot::create(entries.as_slice());\n   376\t        match self.storage.get_snapshot()? {\n   377\t            Some(mut s) => {\n   378\t                s.merge(delta);\n   379\t                Ok(s)\n   380\t            }\n   381\t            None => Ok(delta),\n   382\t        }\n   383\t    }\n   384\t\n   385\t    // Creates a Delta snapshot of entries from `from_idx` to the end of the decided log and also\n   386\t    // returns the compacted idx of the created snapshot. If the range of entries contains entries\n   387\t    // which have already been compacted a valid delta cannot be created, so creates a Complete\n   388\t    // snapshot of the entire decided log instead.\n   389\t    pub(crate) fn create_diff_snapshot(\n   390\t        &self,\n   391\t        from_idx: usize,\n   392\t    ) -> StorageResult<(Option<SnapshotType<T>>, usize)> {\n   393\t        let log_decided_idx = self.get_decided_idx_without_stopsign();\n   394\t        let compacted_idx = self.get_compacted_idx();\n   395\t        let snapshot = if from_idx <= compacted_idx {\n     1\tTo change the servers in the cluster, we must first stop the current OmniPaxos cluster. This is done via the `reconfigure()` function, which takes a `ClusterConfig` that contains the settings for the next OmniPaxos cluster and some optional metadata.\n     2\t\n     3\t```rust\n     4\t// Node 3 seems to have crashed... let's replace it with a new node 4.\n     5\tlet new_configuration = ClusterConfig {\n     6\t    configuration_id: 2,\n     7\t    nodes: vec![1, 2, 4],\n     8\t    ..Default::default()\n     9\t};\n    10\tlet metadata = None;\n    11\tomni_paxos.reconfigure(new_configuration, metadata).expect(\"Failed to propose reconfiguration\");\n    12\t```\n    13\t\n    14\tCalling ``reconfigure()`` will propose a `StopSign` entry to be appended. If it gets decided, the log is sealed and prevented from being further appended. From the `StopSign` entry, all nodes will be able to see the new configuration. When you, the user, read from a node and find a `LogEntry::StopSign` in the log, you should start a new `OmniPaxos` instance at this node if it is part of the new configuration.\n    15\t\n    16\t```rust\n    17\t    // the ServerConfig config for current node\n    18\t    let current_config = ServerConfig {\n    19\t        pid: 2,\n    20\t        ..Default::default()\n    21\t    };\n    22\t    let my_pid = current_config.pid;\n    23\t    \n    24\t    let idx: usize = 2;  // some index we last read from\n    25\t    let decided_entries: Option<Vec<LogEntry<KeyValue>>> = omni_paxos.read_decided_suffix(idx);\n    26\t\n    27\t    if let Some(de) = decided_entries {\n    28\t        for d in de {\n    29\t            match d {\n    30\t                LogEntry::StopSign(stopsign, true) => {\n    31\t                    let new_configuration = stopsign.next_config;\n    32\t                    if new_configuration.nodes.contains(&my_pid) {\n    33\t                        // current configuration has been safely stopped. Start new instance\n    34\t                        let new_storage = MemoryStorage::default();\n    35\t                        let mut new_omnipaxos = new_configuration.build_for_server(current_config.clone(), MemoryStorage::default()).unwrap();\n    36\t\n    37\t                        // use new_omnipaxos\n    38\t                        // ...\n    39\t                    }\n    40\t                }\n    41\t                _ => {}\n    42\t            }\n    43\t        }\n    44\t    }\n    45\t```\n    46\t\n    47\t> **Note:** New nodes will not see the `StopSign` since they were not part of the old configuration. The user themselves must notify and start these new nodes. Furthermore,the user must ensure these new nodes have the application state or log up to the stopsign before starting their `OmniPaxos` instance.\n     1\tYou are free to use any storage implementation with `OmniPaxos`. The only requirement is that it implements the `Storage` trait. OmniPaxos includes the package `omnipaxos_storage` which provides two types of storage implementation that work out of the box: `MemoryStorage` and `PersistentStorage`.\n     2\t\n     3\t## Importing `omnipaxos_storage`\n     4\tTo use the provided storage implementations, we need to add `omnipaxos_storage` to the dependencies in the cargo file. You can find the latest version on [crates](https://crates.io/crates/omnipaxos_storage).\n     5\t```toml\n     6\t[dependencies]\n     7\tomnipaxos_storage = { version = \"LATEST_VERSION\", default-features = true }\n     8\t```\n     9\t\n    10\t**If** you **do** decide to implement your own storage, we recommend taking a look at `MemoryStorage` as a reference for implementing the functions required by `Storage`.\n    11\tUpon receiving a `StorageResult::Error(_)` from the storage implementation, Omnipaxos tries to roll back incomplete changes, to enable crash-recovery, and then panicks.\n    12\t\n    13\t## MemoryStorage\n    14\t`MemoryStorage` is an in-memory storage implementation and it will be used in our examples. For simplicity, we leave out some parts of the implementation for now (such as [Snapshots](../compaction)).\n    15\t```rust\n    16\t// from the module omnipaxos_storage::memory_storage\n    17\t#[derive(Clone)]\n    18\tpub struct MemoryStorage<T>\n    19\twhere\n    20\t    T: Entry,\n    21\t{\n    22\t    /// Vector which contains all the replicated entries in-memory.\n    23\t    log: Vec<T>,\n    24\t    /// Last promised round.\n    25\t    n_prom: Ballot,\n    26\t    /// Last accepted round.\n    27\t    acc_round: Ballot,\n    28\t    /// Length of the decided log.\n    29\t    ld: usize,\n    30\t    /// Garbage collected index.\n    31\t    trimmed_idx: usize,\n    32\t    ...\n    33\t}\n    34\t\n    35\timpl<T> Storage<T> for MemoryStorage<T>\n    36\t    where\n    37\t    T: Entry,\n    38\t{\n    39\t    fn write_atomically(&mut self, ops: Vec<StorageOp<T>>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    40\t        for op in ops {\n    41\t            match op {\n    42\t                StorageOp::AppendEntry(entry) => self.append_entry(entry)?,\n    43\t                StorageOp::AppendEntries(entries) => self.append_entries(entries)?,\n    44\t                StorageOp::AppendOnPrefix(from_idx, entries) => {\n    45\t                    self.append_on_prefix(from_idx, entries)?\n    46\t                }\n    47\t                StorageOp::SetPromise(bal) => self.set_promise(bal)?,\n    48\t                StorageOp::SetDecidedIndex(idx) => self.set_decided_idx(idx)?,\n    49\t                StorageOp::SetAcceptedRound(bal) => self.set_accepted_round(bal)?,\n    50\t                ...\n    51\t            }\n    52\t        }\n    53\t        Ok(())\n    54\t    }\n    55\t\n    56\t    fn append_entry(&mut self, entry: T) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    57\t        self.log.push(entry);\n    58\t        Ok(())\n    59\t    }\n    60\t\n    61\t    fn append_entries(&mut self, entries: Vec<T>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    62\t        let mut e = entries;\n    63\t        self.log.append(&mut e);\n    64\t        Ok(())\n    65\t    }\n    66\t\n    67\t    fn append_on_prefix(&mut self, from_idx: usize, entries: Vec<T>) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    68\t        self.log.truncate(from_idx - self.trimmed_idx);\n    69\t        self.append_entries(entries)\n    70\t    }\n    71\t\n    72\t    fn set_promise(&mut self, n_prom: Ballot) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    73\t        self.n_prom = Some(n_prom);\n    74\t        Ok(())\n    75\t    }\n    76\t\n    77\t    fn set_decided_idx(&mut self, ld: usize) -> StorageResult<()> {\n    78\t        self.ld = ld;\n    79\t        Ok(())\n    80\t    }\n     1\tWe now show how to read and write the replicated log. The replicated log is *append-only*. To append an entry we call the following:\n     2\t\n     3\t```rust\n     4\tlet write_entry = KeyValue { key: String::from(\"a\"), value: 123 };\n     5\tomni_paxos.append(write_entry).expect(\"Failed to append\");\n     6\t```\n     7\t\n     8\tThis will cause our `write_entry` to be proposed to get decided in the replicated log. Appends can be pipelined without waiting for preceding entries to be decided. Furthermore, `append()` can be called on any node. If the calling node is not the leader, the entry will be forwarded. \n     9\t\n    10\t## Reading the Log\n    11\tReads are also handled by calling various functions on `OmniPaxos`. To read the entry at a specific index `idx` of the log we call `omni_paxos.read_entry(idx)`. We can also read a specific range of log entries with `omni_paxos.read_entries()`. \n    12\t\n    13\t```rust\n    14\t/*** Read a single entry ***/\n    15\tlet idx = 5;\n    16\tlet read_entry = omni_paxos.read(idx);\n    17\t\n    18\t/*** Read a range ***/\n    19\tlet read_entries = omni_paxos.read_entries(2..5);\n    20\t``` \n    21\t\n    22\tThe read functions return `Option<LogEntry>` and `Option<Vec<LogEntry>>` respectively, where `None` is returned if the index or range is out of bounds. `LogEntry` is an enum with the following variants:\n    23\t- `Decided(T)`: The entry is decided and guaranteed to not be reverted. It is thus safe to apply a decided entry to the application state. For instance, in our case, it is safe to update our key-value store when we read a `Decided(KeyValue)` entry.\n    24\t- `Undecided(T)`: The entry is NOT decided and might be removed from the log at a later time. However, it could be useful in applications that allow speculative execution for example.\n    25\t- `Trimmed(TrimmedIndex)`: We tried to read an index where the entry has already been trimmed. \n    26\t- `Snapshotted(SnapshottedEntry<T>)`: The index we read has already been compacted into a snapshot. We can access the snapshot from the field `snapshot` in `SnapshottedEntry`. In our case our this will correspond to `KVSnapshot` that we defined [here](../compaction).\n    27\t- `StopSign(StopSign)`: This Sequence Paxos instance has been stopped for reconfiguration. This implies that this log will not be appended anymore and one should use the new Sequence Paxos instead for writing.\n    28\t\n    29\tIt is also possible to only read decided entries or snapshot from a specific index using `read_decided_suffix(idx)`.\n    30\t\n    31\t\n    32\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
