"consumes_fact_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Consumes Fact Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"cross_activity_effects\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"description\": \"Activity ID to a concrete semantic effect description; not feeds, Behavior IDs or an inferred fact guarantee\", \"propertyNames\": {\"enum\": [\"A1\", \"A2\", \"A3\", \"A4\", \"A5\", \"A6\", \"A7\"]}, \"title\": \"Cross Activity Effects\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"existing_protections\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Existing Protections\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"source_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unknowns\": {\"description\": \"Unresolved implementation or interface relationships; check exclusions and execution progress belong to Scope/CheckRun\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unknowns\", \"type\": \"array\"}}\nCoreOverview required ['rationale']\n{\"formation\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CorePath\"}, \"context\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CorePath\"}, \"connection\": {\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/CorePath\"}, \"open_details\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Open Details\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"core_gaps\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Core Gaps\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"status\": {\"default\": \"incomplete\", \"enum\": [\"incomplete\", \"usable\", \"blocked\"], \"title\": \"Status\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"rationale\": {\"title\": \"Rationale\", \"type\": \"string\"}}\nCorePath required None\n{\"explanation\": {\"default\": \"\", \"title\": \"Explanation\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"behavior_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Behavior Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"fact_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Fact Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"source_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}}\nFact required ['id', 'meaning', 'identity', 'validity_context', 'representation', 'durability', 'recovery', 'source_ids']\n{\"id\": {\"title\": \"Id\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"meaning\": {\"title\": \"Meaning\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"identity\": {\"additionalProperties\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Identity\", \"type\": \"object\"}, \"established_by\": {\"description\": \"Derived from Behavior.produces_fact_ids; never infer an unread producer\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Established By\", \"type\": \"array\", \"x-controller-derived\": true}, \"consumed_by\": {\"description\": \"Derived from Behavior.consumes_fact_ids\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Consumed By\", \"type\": \"array\", \"x-controller-derived\": true}, \"validity_context\": {\"title\": \"Validity Context\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"representation\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Representation\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"invalidators\": {\"description\": \"Existing Behavior IDs only. Unread events or suspected invalidators belong in unknowns.\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Invalidators\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"reinterpreters\": {\"description\": \"Existing Behavior IDs only, not event descriptions or Activity IDs.\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Reinterpreters\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"durability\": {\"title\": \"Durability\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"recovery\": {\"title\": \"Recovery\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_ids\": {\"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"minItems\": 1, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unknowns\": {\"description\": \"Unknown establishment, consumption or validity in this implementation; known weak guarantees belong to meaning/context/durability\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unknowns\", \"type\": \"array\"}}\nSurface required ['entry_point', 'disposition', 'reason']\n{\"entry_point\": {\"title\": \"Entry Point\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"disposition\": {\"enum\": [\"mapped\", \"externalized\", \"infrastructure\", \"deferred\", \"UNCLASSIFIED_PROTOCOL_RESPONSIBILITY\"], \"title\": \"Disposition\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"behavior_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Behavior Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"reason\": {\"title\": \"Reason\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"source_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"high_consequence\": {\"default\": false, \"title\": \"High Consequence\", \"type\": \"boolean\"}}\nTargetProfile required ['system_boundary']\n{\"system_boundary\": {\"title\": \"System Boundary\", \"type\": \"string\"}, \"protocol_contexts\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Protocol Contexts\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"external_interfaces\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"External Interfaces\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"ownership\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Ownership\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"selection_injection\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Selection Injection\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"variants\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Variants\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"source_ids\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Source Ids\", \"type\": \"array\"}, \"unknowns\": {\"default\": [], \"items\": {\"type\": \"string\"}, \"title\": \"Unknowns\", \"type\": \"array\"}}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > build_initial.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nsources=[]\ndef src(i,f,a,b,k='code_observation'):\n sources.append(dict(id=i,file=f,start_line=a,end_line=b,kind=k));return i\nL=src('M-leader','omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/leader.rs',14,415)\nF=src('M-follower','omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/follower.rs',13,289)\nS=src('M-sequence','omnipaxos/src/sequence_paxos/mod.rs',22,437)\nQ=src('M-accounting','omnipaxos/src/util.rs',96,259)\nE=src('M-election','omnipaxos/src/ballot_leader_election.rs',164,294)\nP=src('M-public','omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs',315,423)\nC=src('M-config','omnipaxos/src/omni_paxos.rs',92,149)\nH=src('M-sync-storage','omnipaxos/src/storage/internal_storage.rs',313,359)\nR=src('M-reconfiguration-doc','docs/omnipaxos/reconfiguration.md',1,47,'document_statement')\nD=src('M-log-doc','docs/omnipaxos/log.md',1,29,'document_statement')\nN=src('M-network-doc','docs/omnipaxos/communication.md',1,26,'document_statement')\nB=[]\ndef behavior(i,a,owner,ctx,trigger,ss,**kw):\n B.append(dict(id=i,primary_activity=a,execution_owner=owner,protocol_context=ctx,trigger=trigger,source_ids=ss,unknowns=[],**kw))\nbehavior('B-prepare','A2','SequencePaxos handle_leader and handle_prepare','Configuration-local ordered ballot and prepare phase','A newer local election or incoming Prepare',[L,F,Q],implementation_guards=['Local election must exceed leader ballot and storage promise; follower accepts higher promise or equal promise in Recover.'],writes=['New local leader resets LeaderState, flushes batches, persists promise, records own promise and enters Prepare. Follower flushes batches, persists promise, enters Prepare and resets sequence number.'],external_effects=['Local leader queues Prepare to peers; follower queues and caches Promise carrying prior accepted round and indices with conditional log suffix.'],produces_fact_ids=['F-promise'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Prepare gathers prior accepted histories to constrain the next leader log.'})\nbehavior('B-formation','A1','SequencePaxos leader handlers and LeaderState','One leader ballot, Prepare then Accept','Matching Promise, local proposal or Accepted',[L,Q],implementation_guards=['Promises counted per sender slot; preparation requires configured quorum. Accepted is consumed only in Leader/Accept with matching ballot.'],writes=['On prepare quorum choose maximum prior accepted history, sync storage with maximum reported decided index, append buffered proposals unless stopped, record own accepted index, enter Accept.','Accepted overwrites sender index; is_chosen counts indexes at least the reported index; qualifying new index updates decided index.'],external_effects=['Queue AcceptSync for promised followers, AcceptDecide for proposals, and Decide or piggyback decision after quorum.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-promise'],async_boundaries=['Outgoing messages require caller extraction and delivery; append return is proposal admission, not decision.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Only matching-ballot replies advance this leader; a new leader initializes fresh accounting.','A5':'Decision index is propagated for later application reads.'})\nbehavior('B-accept','A1','SequencePaxos follower handlers','Promised ballot and follower phase/session','AcceptSync, AcceptDecide, AcceptStopSign or Decide',[F],implementation_guards=['AcceptSync requires equal promise and Follower/Prepare. AcceptDecide and StopSign require Follower/Accept plus expected sequence; Decide requires Accept phase plus expected sequence.'],writes=['AcceptSync synchronizes history then enters Accept and installs sequence. Ordered accepts append; decided-index update may flush batching and caps new decision by available accepted index in that branch.'],external_effects=['Accepted replies are queued or coalesced after completed storage calls; synchronization forwards buffered proposals if no StopSign.'],consumes_fact_ids=['F-promise'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Stale ballot is rejected with NotAccepted; unexpected higher ballot requests recovery.'})\nbehavior('B-recovery','A3','SequencePaxos construction, reconnect and retry handlers','Persisted promise and reconnecting peer','Stored promise at construction, reconnected callback, sequence gap or resend timeout',[S,F,L],writes=['Stored promise starts Recover; reconnect to current leader enters Recover; leader PrepareReq resets sender promise and latest accept metadata.'],external_effects=['PrepareReq prompts Prepare; follower retries cached Promise or recovery PrepareReq. Leader retries Prepare and StopSign/StopSign decision as appropriate.'],cross_activity_effects={'A2':'Equal-ballot Prepare is re-admitted in Recover.','A1':'Recovery establishes synchronized log before accepting subsequent ordered work.'})\nbehavior('B-ble','A2','BallotLeaderElection and OmniPaxos tick','Heartbeat round, configuration ID, ballot','Heartbeat request/reply and election timeout',[E,P],implementation_guards=['Heartbeat reply checks round and ballot configuration ID.'],writes=['Replies are appended to a vector; happiness counts potential followers, using write quorum in Leader/Accept and read quorum otherwise; unhappy quorum-connected node increments ballot.'],external_effects=['Queue heartbeat messages; timeout can select local ballot for SequencePaxos.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'BLE selection still requires SequencePaxos prepare promises before formation.'})\nbehavior('B-sync-storage','A6','InternalStorage::sync_log','Accepted round, decided prefix, optional suffix/snapshot/StopSign','Leader prepare quorum or follower AcceptSync',[H],writes=['Updates cache and issues write_atomically with round/decision plus optional trim, snapshot, prefix replacement and StopSign operations.'],cross_activity_effects={'A1':'Installs history used for subsequent accepted acknowledgments.','A2':'Associates installed history with accepted ballot.'})\nroles=[('A1','Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement','Promise quorum selects history; matching Accepted quorum advances decision.',[L,F,Q]),('A2','Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority','BLE proposes leadership; persisted promises, phase and sequence checks constrain work.',[L,F,E]),('A3','Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation','Stored promise and reconnect enter recovery, with PrepareReq/Prepare/Promise/AcceptSync handshake.',[S,F,L]),('A4','Configuration and participant eligibility','Configuration controls peer set and quorum sizes; StopSign selects next configuration.',[C,R]),('A5','Decision application and consumption','Read APIs expose decided log to callers; application must use decided entries.',[P,D]),('A6','History, persistence and reconstruction of support','InternalStorage synchronizes history through Storage::write_atomically; backend implementations remain to read.',[H]),('A7','Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion','Append admits proposals; caller fetches messages and reads decided results. In-repository runtime completion behavior remains unread.',[P,D,N])]\nactivities=[dict(class_id=a,applicability='applicable',purpose=p,realization_summary=r,source_ids=ss) for a,p,r,ss in roles]\nformation='Append is proposal admission: followers forward or buffer, leaders buffer in Prepare or append in Accept. A new leader gathers sender-indexed promises, selects the maximum accepted history and maximum reported decision index, synchronizes storage, then sends AcceptSync. Followers acknowledge synchronized or appended log indices. The leader counts per-sender accepted indices for its ballot and advances decisions when the configured write quorum supports an index. Decide/AcceptDecide propagate the index; public reads distinguish Decided from Undecided and applications consume the former.'\ncontext='BLE uses heartbeat rounds and configuration-tagged ballots to select leadership. SequencePaxos independently requires a ballot higher than its existing leader and promise. A local leader resets volatile quorum accounting and persists its promise; a receiving follower persists a higher promise and enters Prepare. Accept processing requires the promised ballot and appropriate phase, and ordered messages use session/counter sequence numbers. Older requests are rejected or ignored; higher unexpected accepts and sequence gaps initiate recovery. Persisted promises start recovery after reconstruction. NotAccepted marks a peer as having promised higher.'\nconnection='Authority is insufficient without prepare support: prior accepted rounds and lengths determine the history installed in the new ballot, while prior decisions constrain the reported decision prefix. Buffered proposals are incorporated after history selection unless a StopSign is present; follower synchronization forwards buffered proposals if not stopped. Old-ballot acknowledgments cannot advance a new leader because accepted handlers require matching ballots and leader state is reset. Recovery reuses equal-ballot Prepare only in Recover and starts a new accept sequence session. StopSign travels with synchronized history and stops new local admission; starting the next configuration and carrying application history is a documented caller duty.'\nspec=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured OmniPaxos Rust implementation, bundled storage and runtime; initial pass covers core synchronous library. Runtime and concrete storage are not externalized merely because interfaces are injectable.',protocol_contexts=['Configuration ID, ordered ballot, role/phase, per-follower sequence session, accepted and decided prefixes'],external_interfaces=['append, handle_incoming, take_outgoing_messages, tick, reconnected, read_decided_suffix, reconfigure, Storage'],source_ids=[P,S,H,R,D,N]),activities=activities,behaviors=B,facts=[dict(id='F-promise',meaning='The replica records its current promised ballot; acce